# The commonest spelling: `node.kind === 3 || node.kind === 5 || ..`: the walk folds a subject that each test reads anew by one name off one holder and reads it once; the scan took each read for a value of its own, so every test began a new run and nothing was saved: ten tests weighed twenty and the helper stayed a call in every turn. The subject of a run is now the holder and the name: in a loop the chain weighs its one read and half its cases, and countLoud() holds the Switch and no call. Outside loops nothing changes: once() calls it.
# f1 = isLoud, f2 = countLoud, f3 = once
